            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "Does this change any behavior ?  Let's assume your client has both an IPV6 and IPV4 address. Right now, if you give it the IPV4 address, does it resolve to the IPV6?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "The intent is that this functionally doesn't change behavior.  Internally it bypasses a dbus call.\n\nFor that specific case, I haven't tested, but would it matter either way?  If it does resolve to IPv6, I would argue that's wrong.  If the user specified IPv4 they intended to connect with IPv4.  Even if IPv6 can represent an ipv4 address, wouldn't the \"right\" thing be to connect with what the user asked for?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "> For that specific case, I haven't tested, but would it matter either way? \n\nI don't think it should matter.. Just wanted to make sure we didn't assume some behavior that is changing here. Overall I am good here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 11,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "\ud83d\udc4d. Sounds good."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_client.hpp",
                    "line": 175,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "hostType ? \nI'm not a big fan of 1 or 2 char variables.. Specially when they aren't well known. It makes searching code harder and makes understanding code harder."
                },
                {
                    "file": "http/http_client.hpp",
                    "line": 175,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "Fair, changed to hostType."
                }
